200\\\",\\\"ms\\\":182,\\\"bytes\\\":7568,\\\"summary\\\":\\\"Session 4314D3… · user F755C2… · 1 action, 1 item  ·  sent without units — cgm.bolus.Session.trend: UnitsNet has no quantity of dimension [metre]^-3[kilogram][second]^-1 (+2 more)\\\",\\\"body\\\":\\\"<Response>\\\\r\\\\n  <Status>OK</Status>\\\\r\\\\n  <Seraphim.Internet.Session Key=\\\\\\\"4314D3C14BCF6E2A\\\\\\\">\\\\r\\\\n    <Variables>\\\\r\\\\n      <User>F755C288F9ABEC0A</User>\\\\r\\\\n      <Site>ABD870A3B5091A73</Site>\\\\r\\\\n      <CreationDate Collapse=\\\\\\\"Earliest\\\\\\\">9/19/2026 9:06:25 AM</CreationDate>\\\\r\\\\n      <LastTouched Collapse=\\\\\\\"Latest\\\\\\\">9/19/2026 9:06:25 AM</LastTouched>\\\\r\\\\n      <DeliverySpeed Unit=\\\\\\\"m/s\\\\\\\" Collapse=\\\\\\\"Monotone\\\\\\\">12.46</DeliverySpeed>\\\\r\\\\n      <Driver Collapse=\\\\\\\"Vote\\\\\\\">Gonk</Driver>\\\\r\\\\n      <Deliveries Collapse=\\\\\\\"Sum\\\\\\\">16</Deliveries>\\\\r\\\\n    </Variables>\\\\r\\\\n    <Actions>\\\\r\\\\n      <Action Key=\\\\\\\"2DC01574B27C4594\\\\\\\" />\\\\r\\\\n    </Actions>\\\\r\\\\n    <Items>\\\\r\\\\n      <Item Key=\\\\\\\"FC43B74DDCE41908\\\\\\\" />\\\\r\\\\n    </Items>\\\\r\\\\n  </Seraphim.Internet.Session>\\\\r\\\\n</Response>\\\",\\\"sent\\\":\\\"<?xml version=\\\\\\\"1.0\\\\\\\" encoding=\\\\\\\"utf-8\\\\\\\"?><xaiml version=\\\\\\\"1\\\\\\\"><name>CGM Bolus Advisor</name><gorp name=\\\\\\\"CGM Bolus Advisor\\\\\\\"><comment view=\\\\\\\"class\\\\\\\">Everything the arithmetic needs, in one model, because SAI allows one model on an algorithm's port.\\\\n\\\\nSession holds the CGM reading — glucose in mg/dL and the trend in mg/dL per minute, which is what a continuous monitor gives you that a finger stick does not — beside the therapy settings it has to be read against: target, low threshold, insulin sensitivity, carbohydrate ratio, insulin already on board and a maximum dose.\\\\n\\\\nMorning is a data instance of Session with one plausible breakfast in it. Advise reads Session and writes Dose.\\\\n\\\\nTwo measurements worth looking at. The trend is \\\\\\\\milli\\\\\\\\gram\\\\\\\\deci\\\\\\\\litre\\\\\\\\tothe{-1}\\\\\\\\minute\\\\\\\\tothe{-1} — a rate written with negative exponents rather than \\\\\\\\per, so it grades Platinum and still reads as mg/dL/min on the chip. And an insulin unit has no SI dimension at all, so every dose row is declared \\\\\\\\one: sensitivity is \\\\\\\"mg/dL per unit\\\\\\\", and per a dimensionless count that is just mg/dL.</comment><expect>Check finds nothing — 0 errors, 0 warnings — so Run is available, and Run comes back OK. (xmlIT reads the body and d…\\\"}]}]}\",\"notesX\":0.0,\"notesY\":0.0,\"notesW\":320.0,\"notesH\":180.0,\"notesOpen\":false,\"runsX\":0.0,\"runsY\":0.0,\"runsW\":380.0,\"runsH\":320.0,\"runsOpen\":false,\"runsRaw\":false,\"runsNoWrap\":false,\"runsFolds\":\"\",\"runsScrollY\":0.0,\"notesScrollY\":0.0,\"lockedPath\":\"\",\"lockedUnitTest\":false,\"wireDSi\":false,\"endpointOpen\":false}"},{"baseId":"AiDesignerApp_77b49567","customData":"{\"uml\":\"{\\\"xmlPanelOpen\\\":false,\\\"xmlPanelWidth\\\":320.0,\\\"xmlViewMode\\\":\\\"Tree\\\"}\",\"endpoint\":\"\",\"statePaneHeight\":240.0,\"view\":\"Class\",\"selected\":\"\",\"libraryCollapsed\":\"\",\"librarySort\":\"\",\"runs\":\"{\\\"designs\\\":[]}\",\"notesX\":64.998046875,\"notesY\":0.0,\"notesW\":389.5296630859375,\"notesH\":402.90386962890625,\"notesOpen\":true,\"runsX\":0.0,\"runsY\":0.0,\"runsW\":380.0,\"runsH\":320.0,\"runsOpen\":false,\"runsRaw\":false,\"runsNoWrap\":false,\"runsFolds\":\"\",\"runsScrollY\":0.0,\"notesScrollY\":7.15740966796875,\"lockedPath\":\"\",\"lockedUnitTest\":false,\"wireDSi\":false,\"endpointOpen\":false}"},{"baseId":"AiDesignerApp_26b56199","customData":"{\"uml\":\"{\\\"xmlPanelOpen\\\":false,\\\"xmlPanelWidth\\\":320.0,\\\"xmlViewMode\\\":\\\"Tree\\\"}\",\"endpoint\":\"\",\"statePaneHeight\":240.0,\"view\":\"Class\",\"selected\":\"\",\"libraryCollapsed\":\"\",\"librarySort\":\"\",\"runs\":\"{